      doc: '<p>Strings are expected to represent a time interval in one of the time formats\nRobot Framework supports:</p>\n<ul>\n<li>a number representing seconds like <code>42</code> or <code>10.5</code></li>\n<li>a "time string" like <code>1 hour 2 seconds</code> or <code>1h 2s</code></li>\n<li>a "timer string" like <code>01:02</code> (1 minute 2 seconds) or <code>01:00:03</code> (1 hour 3 seconds)</li>\n</ul>\n<p>Integers and floats are considered to be seconds.</p>\n<p>See the <a href="https://robotframework.org/robotframework/latest/RobotFrameworkUserGuide.html#time-format">User Guide</a> for more details about the supported time formats.</p>',
